  #line-at(138.96pt, 575.7pt, "INTRODUCTION ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 591.241pt, "The increasing computational demand of artificial intelligence ")
  #line-at(46.786pt, 603.305pt, "(AI) has spurred extensive research into developing emerging ")
  #line-at(46.766pt, 615.369pt, "memory devices for novel computing paradigms. Numerous ")
  #line-at(46.756pt, 627.433pt, "types of memories, such as resistive random access memory ")
  #line-at(46.746pt, 639.497pt, "(RRAM), phase change memory (PCM), and ferroelectric field-")
  #line-at(46.746pt, 651.622pt, "effect transistor (FeFET) have been actively investigated for ")
  #line-at(46.746pt, 663.686pt, "applications in current domain compute-in-memory (CIM) [1]. ")
  #line-at(46.716pt, 675.75pt, "More recently, non-volatile capacitive memory (nvCAP) has ")
  #line-at(46.716pt, 687.814pt, "emerged as a promising memory candidate for next-generation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 721.44pt, "This work was supported by PRISM and CHIMES, two of the ")
  #line-at(46.801pt, 730.617pt, "semiconductor research corporation (SRC) centers. The authors are with the ")
  #line-at(46.801pt, 739.858pt, "School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Georgia Institute of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.2pt, 468.48pt, "charge-domain CIM [2-5]. The foundational principle of ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 480.544pt, "nvCAP is its AC small signal capacitance memory window at ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 492.608pt, "0V. Such a mechanism allows non-destructive read-out of the ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 504.672pt, "two capacitance states (C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.72pt, 505.68pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(427.2pt, 504.66pt, ", C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
