  #line-at(56.876pt, 507.301pt, "The ALD IWO nvCAP used in this study is fabricated ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 519.365pt, "following the process flow described in Fig. 3(a). W ")
  #line-at(46.776pt, 531.429pt, "concentration is optimized to 4 at.% in the ALD super-cycling ")
  #line-at(46.766pt, 543.553pt, "scheme established in our previous work [6]. In this study, we ")
  #line-at(46.756pt, 555.617pt, "adopt an improved ferroelectric process over prior work [6] for ")
  #line-at(46.776pt, 567.681pt, "enhanced ferroelectric performance (larger P")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(232.2pt, 568.68pt, "r")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(234.36pt, 567.66pt, "). Sacrificial W ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 579.724pt, "layer thickness is increased from 80 nm to 130 nm to achieve ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 591.848pt, "better ferroelectric properties by applying larger mechanical ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 603.912pt, "stress to the HZO layer during the annealing process [13]. Fig. ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 615.976pt, "3(b) shows the comparison of the P-V characteristics of an ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 628.041pt, "nvCAP with symmetric TE/BE between the prior work and this ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 640.165pt, "work. Here, the symmetric TE/BE design is compared to ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 652.229pt, "exclude the impact of the channel resistance on P-V ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 664.293pt, "characteristics. A higher P")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(154.02pt, 665.28pt, "r ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(158.16pt, 664.26pt, "is achieved in this work due to the ")
  #line-at(46.788pt, 676.324pt, "improved process. In the following sections, we examine the ")
  #line-at(46.788pt, 688.388pt, "pulse-mode operation of nvCAPs with asymmetric TE/BE ")
  #line-at(46.788pt, 700.512pt, "designs, which exhibit higher C")
