  #line-at(46.8pt, 532.332pt, "region.  ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 543.855pt, "    Furthermore, Fig. 7(d)-(e) highlights the effect of wake-up ")
  #line-at(46.78pt, 555.318pt, "conditions on C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(109.98pt, 556.32pt, "on ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.02pt, 555.3pt, "and C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.66pt, 556.32pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.22pt, 555.3pt, ". Stronger wake-up conditions lead to ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 566.823pt, "a larger number of woken up FE domains resulting in more a ")
  #line-at(46.796pt, 578.346pt, "conductive channel in the non-overlap region, increasing C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.26pt, 579.36pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.797pt, 589.803pt, "retention. At the same time, a larger number of FE domains are ")
  #line-at(46.797pt, 601.326pt, "partially erased after ERS, becoming the cause of longer read-")
  #line-at(46.797pt, 612.849pt, "after-delay.  ")
  #line-at(46.807pt, 624.312pt, "    Lastly, retention characteristics at elevated temperature ")
  #line-at(46.807pt, 635.835pt, "(85 °C) are examined (Fig. 7(f)). Faster decay of C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(257.1pt, 636.84pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(263.58pt, 635.82pt, " and C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.12pt, 636.84pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.797pt, 647.343pt, "compared to 25 °C under an identical device geometry (Fig. ")
  #line-at(46.777pt, 658.806pt, "7(e)) can be attributed to FE layer experiencing accelerated ")
  #line-at(46.777pt, 670.329pt, "back-switching, degraded P")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(160.74pt, 671.34pt, "r")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(162.9pt, 670.32pt, ", pronounced imprint at elevated ")
  #line-at(46.798pt, 681.783pt, "temperature, consistent with prior reports [19-21]. The high ")
  #line-at(46.788pt, 693.306pt, "gate leakage of the FE layer could also contribute to accelerated ")
  #line-at(46.788pt, 704.829pt, "retention loss at elevated temperature [22]. Additionally, initial ")
  #line-at(46.798pt, 716.292pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(53.46pt, 717.3pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(61.02pt, 716.28pt, " value at t=1 s under the same wake-up condition is ")
  #line-at(46.792pt, 727.803pt, "significantly higher than 25 °C case, causing significant read-")
  #line-at(46.792pt, 739.326pt, "after-delay. This read-after-delay is not improved by increasing ")
  #line-at(313.183pt, 371.341pt, "the ERS pulse width, in contrast to the 25 °C case. Such ")
  #line-at(313.183pt, 382.865pt, "phenomenon could be attributed to the increased intrinsic ")
  #line-at(313.183pt, 394.327pt, "carrier concentration of the IWO channel [23]. Higher intrinsic ")
  #line-at(313.193pt, 405.85pt, "carrier concentration at elevated temperatures makes the ERS ")
  #line-at(313.183pt, 417.373pt, "more difficult in the non-overlap region increasing C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(525.06pt, 418.38pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(532.62pt, 417.36pt, ".  ")
  #line-at(313.202pt, 428.823pt, "    Based on the retention analysis of C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.76pt, 429.84pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(474.24pt, 428.82pt, " and C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(500.4pt, 429.84pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(507.96pt, 428.82pt, " under various ")
  #line-at(313.201pt, 440.343pt, "conditions, several knobs for the stable retention of oxide-")
  #line-at(313.211pt, 451.806pt, "channel ferroelectric nvCAPs can be conceived. Retention loss ")
  #line-at(313.221pt, 463.329pt, "of C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(330.42pt, 464.34pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(336.9pt, 463.32pt, " can be minimized by engineering the depolarization field ")
  #line-at(313.213pt, 474.843pt, "from the FE layer, especially in the non-overlap region. This ")
  #line-at(313.213pt, 486.306pt, "can be achieved by increasing the PGM efficiency, for example ")
  #line-at(313.223pt, 497.829pt, "by redesigning the TE geometry (e.g., multi-TE structure) or ")
  #line-at(313.213pt, 509.352pt, "scaling the TE and BE area toward nanometer scale. ")
  #line-at(313.223pt, 520.815pt, "Furthermore, retention-aware gate or channel-stack engineering ")
  #line-at(313.213pt, 532.338pt, "can be considered to improve intrinsic retention of the FE layer. ")
  #line-at(313.213pt, 543.861pt, "Read-after-delay of C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(404.58pt, 544.86pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(412.08pt, 543.84pt, " can be reduced by adopting a new ")
  #line-at(313.203pt, 555.303pt, "device structure that ensures more effective ERS in the non-")
  #line-at(313.203pt, 566.826pt, "overlap region. Alternatively, intrinsic carrier concentration in ")
  #line-at(313.193pt, 578.349pt, "the non-overlap region can be selectively optimized to reduce ")
  #line-at(313.183pt, 589.812pt, "read-after-delay of C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.56pt, 590.82pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(411.12pt, 589.8pt, " at elevated temperature while still ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 601.323pt, "ensuring high C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.1pt, 602.34pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(383.58pt, 601.32pt, " retention.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.2pt, 624.84pt, "B. Write Endurance ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.2pt, 639.299pt, "    Next, we examine the write-endurance characteristics of ")
  #line-at(313.21pt, 650.822pt, "ALD IWO nvCAPs at ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(401.88pt, 650.82pt, "25 °C ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(423.84pt, 650.82pt, "under different geometry and wake-")
  #line-at(313.199pt, 662.343pt, "up conditions. The test sequence is described in Fig. 8(a). The ")
  #line-at(313.189pt, 673.806pt, "write endurance failure point (highlighted in pink font) is ")
  #line-at(313.189pt, 685.329pt, "defined as the cycling count where abrupt drop (>300 % ")
  #line-at(313.179pt, 696.792pt, "decrease from previous cycle count) happens in C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(526.14pt, 697.8pt, "on ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(535.68pt, 696.78pt, "or C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(555.06pt, 697.8pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(562.62pt, 696.78pt, ", ")
  #line-at(313.202pt, 708.303pt, "which is a possible indication of dielectric breakdown leading ")
  #line-at(313.202pt, 719.826pt, "to a sharp increase of the number of oxygen vacancies in HZO ")
  #line-at(313.182pt, 731.289pt, "[24, 25].  ")
