  #line-at(536.82pt, 191.94pt, "against ")
  #line-at(313.204pt, 203.403pt, "positive voltages. While the results demonstrate NDRO of >10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(561.96pt, 199.92pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.197pt, 214.923pt, "read stress cycles, they simultaneously imply there is a desired ")
  #line-at(313.187pt, 226.446pt, "TE/BE configuration of ALD IWO nvCAPs; To maximize read ")
  #line-at(313.187pt, 237.909pt, "endurance, read voltage pulses needs to be applied to “TE” in a ")
  #line-at(313.187pt, 249.432pt, "practical array implementation with positive operating voltage.  ")
  #line-at(403.559pt, 284.457pt, "VII.")
  #line-at(421.98pt, 284.46pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(428.64pt, 284.46pt, "ONCLUSION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.197pt, 299.941pt, "    In this study, we have provided a comprehensive study on the ")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 311.404pt, "pulse-mode writing and reliability (retention, read endurance, ")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 322.927pt, "write endurance) characteristics of oxide-channel ferroelectric ")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 334.45pt, "nvCAPs. We have outlined the governing physics that lead to ")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 345.913pt, "non-ideal behaviors of oxide-channel ferroelectric nvCAPs, ")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 357.436pt, "which provides a foundation for understanding their pulse-")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 368.959pt, "mode operation and reliability characteristics. Using an ALD ")
  #line-at(313.197pt, 380.422pt, "IWO nvCAP with asymmetric TE/BE, we have shown that ")
  #line-at(313.187pt, 391.945pt, "pulse-mode writing characteristics significantly depend on ")
  #line-at(313.187pt, 403.408pt, "wake-up and write pulse conditions, suggesting the need to ")
  #line-at(313.187pt, 414.931pt, "optimize both conditions to target desired C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.54pt, 415.92pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(499.02pt, 414.9pt, " and C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(526.5pt, 415.92pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(534pt, 414.9pt, " values. ")
  #line-at(313.199pt, 426.423pt, "Further, pulse-mode retention results have highlighted (i) the ")
  #line-at(313.199pt, 437.886pt, "role of depolarization field in C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(442.08pt, 438.9pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(448.56pt, 437.88pt, " retention and (ii) the impact ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 449.403pt, "of inherent hole deficiency of the oxide channel on the ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 460.926pt, "pronounced read-after-delay of C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(450.18pt, 461.94pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(457.74pt, 460.92pt, ". Together with the pulse-")
  #line-at(313.211pt, 472.383pt, "mode write endurance results, they have indicated the ")
  #line-at(313.211pt, 483.906pt, "importance of overlap area optimization and device area scaling ")
  #line-at(313.232pt, 495.429pt, "to simultaneously improve C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.08pt, 496.44pt, "on")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(451.56pt, 495.42pt, "/C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(460.98pt, 496.44pt, "off")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.54pt, 495.42pt, ", retention and write ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 506.883pt, "endurance. Lastly, voltage polarity-dependent NDRO has been ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 518.406pt, "examined, demonstrating NDRO for >10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(489.72pt, 514.92pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.96pt, 518.4pt, " stress cycles of ")
  #line-at(313.201pt, 529.923pt, "|V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(322.44pt, 530.94pt, "read")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.6pt, 529.92pt, "|=1 V while suggesting optimal device configuration for ")
  #line-at(313.189pt, 541.383pt, "practical array implementation. The study has offered ")
  #line-at(313.189pt, 552.906pt, "foundational insights into the underlying device physics ")
  #line-at(313.209pt, 564.429pt, "governing the pulse-mode operation of oxide-channel ")
  #line-at(313.199pt, 575.892pt, "ferroelectric nvCAPs. These insights are expected to guide the ")
  #line-at(313.199pt, 587.415pt, "design and operation of oxide-channel ferroelectric nvCAPs ")
  #line-at(313.189pt, 598.938pt, "toward realizing pragmatic BEOL-compatible non-volatile ")
  #line-at(313.179pt, 610.401pt, "capacitive arrays.  ")
